ing benefits like better  sleep and better energy strength mood  mobility and lower risk of chronic  disease why can't we focus the  conversation on that but again we've  seen her very militant and punitive  approach to exercise even going so far  as to basically glorify puking or  passing out never mind pushing through  when it very much does not feel good  this whole no pain no gain approach is  actually the complete opposite message  of this principle moving your body  should be a gift not a punishment  honestly western society is never going  to see improvements in population health  when the barriers to entry are just so  high but again it would probably be  off-brand for her to suggest anything  else  progress not perfection that's what  counts couldn't agree more however this  is also in direct opposition to the what  was it eat whatever the hell you want  unconditional permission to eat what i  don't like is it does negate some of the  basic science of losing weight oh  my f  i feel like i'm taking crazy pills this  is why jillian doesn't actually  understand intuitive eating at all it's  not all or nothing i know this is a huge  paradigm shift for a lot of us who have  been stuck in diet culture for so long  so i'm usually a lot more patient but  i'm just so annoyed that jillian doesn't  do her homework at all like it feels  like a moot point to even try to correct  her because the basis of her arguments  are all grounded in weight loss which  intuitive eating is not about but i will  try to make this as simple as possible  gentle nutrition you need to give  yourself permission to eat what you want  to help silence the noise that prevents  us from objectively collecting data on  how foods make us feel how does food  impact our energy levels mood sleep  digestion what we actually like etc this  is done without judgment moral  association or desire to manipulate our  body then once we've gone through all  these other principles only then can we  even start to think about gentle  nutrition in a way that's not going to  set us back and that contrary to  jillian's comment is in fact supported  by research  all that said it's quite clear that  jillian didn't do a lick of her own  research on intuitive eating and she  couldn't bring herself to put down her  damn weight loss tinted glasses to  attempt to see it for what it actually  is and that is a mind-body framework for  healing one's relationship with food and  it's really too bad because this lazy  youtube video of hers was a missed  opportunity to actually learn about an  evidence-based eating philosophy that  millions of people have benefited from  and after striking out once with her  podcast episode on this i mean you'd  think she would maybe hit the books  before going at it again here but she  basically has a lot of the same  unrehearsed uneducated remarks there but  until jillian can imagine a world where  health is about more than your weight i  do feel that the concept of intuitive  eating will just fall on deaf ears so  please if you guys are truly curious  about intuitive eating go by the book  which i'm gonna link below and watch my  beginners series here and on that note  that is all that i have for you guys  today if you liked it be sure to give it  the thumbs up leave me a comment below  on your thoughts and what you'd like to  see me cover next subscribe to the  channel and i'll see you next time on  abby's kitchen bye  [Music]
 

